  "id": "functional-reorganization",
  "term": "functional reorganization",
  "definition": "Functional reorganization is a change in how brain functions are carried out after damage, shown by activation patterns shifting away from the usual network seen in non-impaired people. In this context, it refers to altered reading or spelling network activity following injury to neural systems involved in orthographic processing.",
